  clock: 3  # 9c23
  nonce: 9c23  # 9c23
  message: "DONE in PR #2274 (dev 7e5d2638a + the install-array fix). The three late gates now run before any tag:\n1. I/O manifest: release-check runs scripts/io-manifest (when strace is installed) on the default package set installed from the built wheels (release.yml's io-manifest set), PATH hidden as the README recipe, IO_MANIFEST_CORPUS_ROOT for existing clones; without strace it warns and names the dry run. prepare-release's handoff now asks for the Release workflow dispatched with dry_run=true on main before tag-release (options (a) and (b) of this item).\n2. Audit: a fresh environment built as release.yml's security-audit (same editable packages, same pins, same ignore list; tests pin the mirror); a failed build fails and never falls back to this box's pip-audit; the box-only diskcache ignore is gone.\n3. Wheels: installed with --find-links dist/ (the default set into a fresh environment; rust-analyzer, scip-python and tracker resolved against it); a failed install or a missing wheel fails. DEFAULT_SET + OTHER_PACKAGES must together name every package (tests/test_release_package_lists.py).\nEVIDENCE. tests/test_release_check_gates.py executes each block extracted from the real script with stub tools; mutations putib/muts.tsv 17 of 17 red. LIVE RUN of the real blocks in a /tmp worktree (putib/live.log, 2026-11-19 05:13-05:15Z): fresh audit environment built and pip-audit clean; 8 wheels built; default set installed, the other three resolved; io-manifest traced the six corpus repositories (existing clones) and matched docs/io-manifest/expected.txt; FAILED=0. LIMIT: the wheels were 10.0.0, already on PyPI, so the live run does not show --find-links resolving an UNPUBLISHED version; the stub test does (its pip fails without --find-links dist/). The next prepare-release is the first real use.\nNOT DONE: option (c), a scheduled run of the io-manifest job; the `chmod <out>/...` line a re-used output directory produces is still in no manifest (noted in the item, not addressed)."  # 9c23
